{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For the tribe of Yosef, for the tribe of Menashe.</b> Even though in other places Yosef is named for Efrayim, here it included the tribe of Menashe, because both of them brought forth an evil report — Yosef against his brothers, and the prince of Menashe against the land. And for this reason, in the portion of Mas'ei and in the book of Yehoshua, Yosef is again named for the tribe of Menashe, because there it speaks of the division of the land, and the evil report was concerning the land. And since the prince of Efrayim did not bring forth an evil report, here it separated them one from the other."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:44.671572976Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}